{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJhSjPiAp1mAhH9vocz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On the original code the new tests reproduce the production error, and with the fix they pass. Now I'm writing ANSWER.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":28507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":514},"output_tokens":62,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed95c658-4374-4077-8b78-83d4c7fb8f1c","uuid":"1e11fcb3-9fd6-4f99-96fa-d645d3d6a181","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:23:23.187Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJhSVW2coq71DBiW8J5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJhSjPiAp1mAhH9vocz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TwkJntHit5wPKSqpnusEyQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xDf4lp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` saves each story along with its top-3 `similar` stories, and each\nof those has a `score` from `similarity()`. That function returns\n`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`, which is a Python **float**,\nand boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n    TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty. `related()` had\nnothing to compare against, so `similar` was `[]`, the item held no floats and\n`put_item` went through (log: `similar=0 stored`, then 201). From the second\npublish on, the table holds a story, so a float score ends up in the item.\n`put_item` then raises and `handler()` turns that into a 500. Every later\npublish fails the same way.\n\nThe bug got past testing because the only test published into an empty table,\nwhich is the one case where no scores are computed.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `src/app.py`: added `to_dynamo()`. It walks the whole item and turns every\n  float into a `Decimal`, going through `str()` so `0.1` stays exactly `0.1`.\n  `publish()` calls it on the complete item just before `put_item`. Because it\n  runs on the whole item at the point of the write, a float in any field,\n  current or added later, gets converted. The bug can't come back by someone\n  adding another computed number.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: added tests that use a table that already has data:\n  - publishing into a table that already has a story (checks the stored\n    `similar` slug and that the score is a `Decimal`);\n  - three publishes in a row through `handler()`, each expected to return 201;\n  - a unit test of `to_dynamo()` on nested floats.\n\n  Run against the original `app.py`, these tests fail with the same\n  `TypeError` as the production log. With the fix, all 4 tests pass\n  (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\nNothing was deployed. To confirm in production, publish two stories in a row\nagainst the real table; the second write is the real test.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":28507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":514},"output_tokens":62,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed95c658-4374-4077-8b78-83d4c7fb8f1c","uuid":"d237015f-d2e4-4c6c-aa6f-efda1de2d048","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:23:29.770Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJhSVW2coq71DBiW8J5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TwkJntHit5wPKSqpnusEyQ":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xDf4lp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` saves each story along with its top-3 `similar` stories, and each\nof those has a `score` from `similarity()`. That function returns\n`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`, which is a Python **float**,\nand boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n    TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty. `related()` had\nnothing to compare against, so `similar` was `[]`, the item held no floats and\n`put_item` went through (log: `similar=0 stored`, then 201). From the second\npublish on, the table holds a story, so a float score ends up in the item.\n`put_item` then raises and `handler()` turns that into a 500. Every later\npublish fails the same way.\n\nThe bug got past testing because the only test published into an empty table,\nwhich is the one case where no scores are computed.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `src/app.py`: added `to_dynamo()`. It walks the whole item and turns every\n  float into a `Decimal`, going through `str()` so `0.1` stays exactly `0.1`.\n  `publish()` calls it on the complete item just before `put_item`. Because it\n  runs on the whole item at the point of the write, a float in any field,\n  current or added later, gets converted. The bug can't come back by someone\n  adding another computed number.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: added tests that use a table that already has data:\n  - publishing into a table that already has a story (checks the stored\n    `similar` slug and that the score is a `Decimal`);\n  - three publishes in a row through `handler()`, each expected to return 201;\n  - a unit test of `to_dynamo()` on nested floats.\n\n  Run against the original `app.py`, these tests fail with the same\n  `TypeError` as the production log. With the fix, all 4 tests pass\n  (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\nNothing was deployed. To confirm in production, publish two stories in a row\nagainst the real table; the second write is the real test.\n"}}}
